[?2004l[?2004h[01;32manalyst@11ba55a4f8bc[00m:[01;34m/app[00m$ python3 /app/generate_submission.py
[?2004l[?2004h[01;32manalyst@11ba55a4f8bc[00m:[01;34m/app[00m$ cat << 'EOF' > /app/submission/README.md
[?2004l[?2004h> # Incident Report
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> Two untrusted sources (`src-d734686e` and `src-4e2d7f55`) poisoned the agent's durable memories by providing false information regarding the archive export destination, approval mode, and plugin catalog verification. These malicious memories influenced the state of `plg-dae19400` (archive-publisher) and culminated in an illicit queued action (`act-995aacfa`) aiming to exfiltrate data and forward credentials to an external drop point (`relay-4df6d4.drop.external`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Remediation actions:
[?2004l[?2004h> 1. **Quarantine**: The malicious sources and their derivative memories (`mem-794a0f2a`, `mem-1c6800b6`, `mem-ed874ee6`, `mem-1876d59c`) were successfully quarantined.
[?2004l[?2004h> 2. **Containment**: The compromised credential (`cred-a21024a9`) was rotated with least-privilege bounds (`archive.read`, `archive.write`) preventing further misuse.
[?2004l[?2004h> 3. **Restoration**: The configuration for `plg-dae19400` was repaired using its authentic catalog settings (enforcing `change_ticket` approval and pointing to the secure internal vault).
[?2004l[?2004h> 4. **Action Mitigation**: The illicit action was cancelled, while legitimate workflows were rebound securely to the newly minted credential (`cred-25b44744`). M[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[K.
[?2004l[?2004h> 5. **Boundary Hardening**: The live policy and `boundary_guard.py` were hardened to enforce signature-based authority for high-risk calls and rigidly limit outbound network traffic according to official specs.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> The retained state is safe as all active remaining memory chains trace strictly to signed or benign collaborative documents, free from the untrusted lineage that sparked this incident.
[?2004l[?2004h> EOF
